IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hesa-help`

-- Higher Education Support Act 2003 (Cth) -- the formulas the first pass could not find, now computed, beside hesa-help.l4
-- (which is left as it was).
--
-- hesa-help.l4 inferred the s 140-25(1) formula, left the s 140-26(2) substitute for 2024-25 unencoded, and took the repayment
-- thresholds after 2025-26 as inputs, because the text deposit dropped the formulas. The sidecar
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A01234.formulas.md gives them:
--   * s 140-25(1): Former accumulated HELP debt + HELP debts incurred - HELP debt repayments - Location-preferred HELP debtor
--     reduction -- the first pass's inference, confirmed;
--   * s 140-26(2), for the financial year starting 1 July 2024: Former accumulated HELP debt + [(HELP debts incurred - HELP debt
--     repayments) x 0.8] - Location-preferred HELP debtor reduction (with s 140-30: cents disregarded, under $1 nil);
--   * s 154-25(2): replacement amount = Indexable amount for the 2025-26 income year x (AWE for the indexation year / AWE for the
--     2025-26 income year), rounded down to the dollar (s 154-25(3));
--   * s 140-10(1A): reduced factor = 1 + ([(A - 1) / 365] x [365 - B]), rounded to 3 places (s 140-10(1), (2)).
-- AWE figures are the Australian Statistician's: inputs. SEAT, edition and method as hesa-help.l4 (naive). See NOTES.md.

§ `Higher Education Support Act -- the first pass's missing formulas, computed`

-- s 140-26(2) with s 140-30.
GIVEN `former accumulated debt` IS A NUMBER, `HELP debts incurred` IS A NUMBER, `HELP debt repayments` IS A NUMBER,
      `location-preferred reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the accumulated HELP debt for 2024-25` MEANS
    IF `before rounding` LESS THAN 1 THEN 0 ELSE FLOOR `before rounding`
    WHERE
        `before rounding` MEANS
            (`former accumulated debt` PLUS ((`HELP debts incurred` MINUS `HELP debt repayments`) TIMES 0.8)) MINUS `location-preferred reduction`

-- s 154-25(2), (3).
GIVEN `indexable amount for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER, `AWE for the indexation year` IS A NUMBER, `AWE for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the replacement amount` MEANS
    FLOOR (`indexable amount for 2025-26` TIMES `AWE for the indexation year` DIVIDED BY `AWE for 2025-26`)

-- The two thresholds for an income year: the stated ones for 2025-26, the replacement amounts after; NOTHING before (the repealed
-- text is not deposited).
GIVEN `income year starting in` IS A NUMBER, `AWE for the indexation year` IS A NUMBER, `AWE for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the minimum repayment income for the year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `income year starting in` LESS THAN 2025 THEN NOTHING
           IF `income year starting in` EQUALS 2025 THEN JUST `the stated minimum repayment income`
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the replacement amount` `the stated minimum repayment income` `AWE for the indexation year` `AWE for 2025-26`)

GIVEN `income year starting in` IS A NUMBER, `AWE for the indexation year` IS A NUMBER, `AWE for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the upper repayment threshold for the year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `income year starting in` LESS THAN 2025 THEN NOTHING
           IF `income year starting in` EQUALS 2025 THEN JUST `the stated upper repayment threshold`
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the replacement amount` `the stated upper repayment threshold` `AWE for the indexation year` `AWE for 2025-26`)

-- The first pass's `the compulsory repayment amount`, with the thresholds worked out for the year (liability under s 154-1 is
-- the first pass's `is liable to a compulsory repayment`, unchanged).
GIVEN `income year starting in` IS A NUMBER, `AWE for the indexation year` IS A NUMBER, `AWE for 2025-26` IS A NUMBER,
      `repayment income` IS A NUMBER, `repayable debt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the compulsory repayment amount for the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the minimum repayment income for the year` `income year starting in` `AWE for the indexation year` `AWE for 2025-26`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST `minimum` THEN
        CONSIDER `the upper repayment threshold for the year` `income year starting in` `AWE for the indexation year` `AWE for 2025-26`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST `upper` THEN JUST (`the compulsory repayment amount` `repayment income` `minimum` `upper` `repayable debt`)

-- s 140-10(1A).
GIVEN `the ordinary factor` IS A NUMBER, `days determined` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reduced HELP debt indexation factor` MEANS
    FLOOR (((1 PLUS (((`the ordinary factor` MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY 365) TIMES (365 MINUS `days determined`))) TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 1000
